mia_cs: Orbit Labs onboarding — they report a short burst of 429s when a new deployment scales up. Using Rust serverless with a small auth sidecar that mints ephemeral tokens per container. Spike lasts ~20s. Any quick mitigations?

oscar_eng: Ask for request ids + headers. Likely sidecar mint stampede or sidecar cold-starts calling our preflight at same time.

mia_cs: Customer logs (sanitized):
```
2024-08-09T07:22:10Z req=or1 POST /v1/embed 200
2024-08-09T07:22:11Z req=or2 POST /v1/embed 429 X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
2024-08-09T07:22:11Z req=or3 POST /v1/embed 429 X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
```

devon_sre: Two pragmatic fixes: (1) Pre-warm a single sidecar per host/container group and have other containers proxy token requests to it; (2) add a tiny randomized init jitter (0-200ms) before the sidecar/microservice fetches tokens so requests don't land simultaneously. Also ensure the sidecar writes a token to /tmp and reuses until expiry.

oscar_eng: For Rust sidecars, use single-flight via once_cell + parking_lot Mutex, example pattern:
```
let jitter = rand::thread_rng().gen_range(0..200);
std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(jitter));
let token = match read_token_from_tmp() {
  Some(t) if !expired(&t) => t,
  _ => {
    let _lock = TOKEN_LOCK.lock();
    // re-check after acquiring
    if let Some(t2) = read_token_from_tmp() { t2 } else { fetch_and_store_token() }
  }
};
```

mia_cs: They also asked if we can loosen server-side short-window enforcement for fresh accounts.

devon_sre: We can consider a manual onboarding quota bump for verified customers for 24-48h, but that's ops-only. For immediate relief, client changes are fastest. Recommend Rust SDK v1.2.0+ which has more robust init backoff — ask them to upgrade.

mia_cs: Can someone paste a 1-paragraph blurb I can send to their SRE?

oscar_eng: "Short-term mitigation for serverless sidecar warmup: (1) Upgrade to Rust SDK v1.2+; (2) implement a per-container /tmp token cache with a single-flight lock to serialize token minting; (3) pre-warm or run a single helper sidecar that other containers proxy to during scale-ups; (4) add randomized init jitter (0-200ms) before the first token fetch; (5) if needed, request a temporary onboarding quota bump from CS. These steps typically eliminate the transient 429 burst without server changes." :thumbsup:

infra-bot: Created ticket CS-7788 to track Rust SDK nudges and onboarding quota flow.

mia_cs: Sent to Orbit Labs, they applied jitter + /tmp cache and saw the 429s disappear. Closing unless they regress. Thanks all.
